    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.animate\n\n### Description\n\nThe tab count for a newly created tab is 2, not 1\n\n### Neovim version\n\n3e569d440b8e5a2b190a7013081d29cb7e04af01\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `minimal.lua`:\r\n\r\n      `require('mini.animate').setup({})`\r\n2. `nvim -u minimal.lua`\r\n3.  `:tab new`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNew tab shows up with a count of 1.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nNew tab shows up with a count of 2.",
