    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is not really an issue with 'mini.animate', but more with how default tabline works. It seems to count *all* windows including floating ones. As 'mini.animate' uses floating windows for \"open\" and \"close\" animation, default tabline counts them when tabpage has just opened or closed. It goes back to counting all visible windows after respective \"open\"/\"close\" animation is finished (and there is some redraw needed; like for example after starting editing buffer).\r\n\r\nIf you don't like this behavior, I'd suggest either using different implementation of tabline or disabling \"open\" and/or \"close\" animation (set corresponding `enable` value(s) to `false`).\r\n\r\nClosing as not an issue with 'mini.animate'.",
